WEBVTT

00:11.390 --> 00:14.740
It feels so nice when you
can head to school early.

00:15.900 --> 00:18.980
We have an English quiz today,
so I'll do some review.

00:18.980 --> 00:22.870
Oh, right. I should get fresh water for
the flowers Satou-san brought, too.

00:24.460 --> 00:27.810
Yes, an excellent start!
Today is sure to be a great day!

00:28.380 --> 00:30.380
Oh, good morning, Iwakura-san.

00:31.110 --> 00:32.570
It's Kanechika-senpai.

00:33.420 --> 00:34.760
How cultured!

00:35.450 --> 00:36.640
Perfect timing.

00:36.640 --> 00:39.050
I wanted to ask you about that guy in your—

00:39.050 --> 00:40.220
I'm sorry!

00:40.670 --> 00:43.570
I'm flattered you said I could
be a memorable star actor

00:43.570 --> 00:45.830
and asked me to join your club,

00:45.830 --> 00:48.680
but I have a different purpose in life...

00:48.680 --> 00:50.320
When did I say all that?

00:51.530 --> 00:54.040
Ah, I see. That's too bad.

00:54.040 --> 00:57.420
But I hope you can fulfill
your purpose in life.

00:57.420 --> 00:58.870
Thank you very much.

00:59.220 --> 01:03.450
Still, without you in our club,
our future is bleak indeed.

01:03.450 --> 01:06.780
I-I'd be happy to help in any way I can!

01:06.780 --> 01:08.930
Really? That'd be great!

01:09.410 --> 01:11.960
This girl's a pushover. I worry for her.

02:42.460 --> 02:45.640
Let's get right to watching this video, then.

02:47.500 --> 02:49.520
An old TV show?

02:49.520 --> 02:50.440
Yeah.

02:50.440 --> 02:55.210
It went up against a super-hit show in the
same time slot and lost the ratings battle,

02:55.210 --> 02:58.400
but it was a simple, good show,
and it still has plenty of hardcore fans.

02:58.780 --> 02:59.110
Huh... But what does it have to...

02:59.110 --> 03:00.910
Can I come hang out tomorrow?
Huh... But what does it have to...

03:02.240 --> 03:04.160
Sh... Shima-kun?!

03:04.160 --> 03:04.730
Wow! He was so cute!

03:04.730 --> 03:06.020
You noticed?
Wow! He was so cute!

03:06.020 --> 03:06.040
Look at his big, round eyes!
He's like an angel!
Wow! He was so cute!

03:06.040 --> 03:07.990
He played Kanade-kun,
the lead's best friend.
Look at his big, round eyes!
He's like an angel!

03:07.990 --> 03:09.030
Wait, what is Shima-kun doing there?
He played Kanade-kun,
the lead's best friend.

03:09.030 --> 03:10.650
He appears in most episodes and
is really... Are you listening?
Wait, what is Shima-kun doing there?

03:10.650 --> 03:12.830
He's so tiny! And cute!
He appears in most episodes and
is really... Are you listening?

03:12.830 --> 03:13.190
He's so tiny! And cute!

03:13.190 --> 03:15.260
What do you think of his acting?

03:16.640 --> 03:19.200
I'm no expert,

03:19.200 --> 03:21.610
but I think it's good.

03:21.610 --> 03:23.430
Why are you always like this, Mom?!
Yeah, he is good.

03:23.430 --> 03:24.650
It's remarkable enough that he could express
such a range of emotions at that age,
Why are you always like this, Mom?!

03:24.650 --> 03:27.460
It's remarkable enough that he could express
such a range of emotions at that age,

03:27.460 --> 03:29.870
but he also did it while understanding
the context of the scene.

03:29.870 --> 03:30.940
Really smart.

03:31.690 --> 03:33.940
Iwakura-san... No, Mitsumi-kun!

03:34.350 --> 03:37.860
Could you convince Shima-kun
to join the drama club?

03:37.860 --> 03:38.820
What?!

03:38.820 --> 03:40.440
I don't know about that...

03:40.440 --> 03:42.590
You two are close, right?

03:42.590 --> 03:45.570
Please help me! I can't
get through to him at all!

03:45.570 --> 03:49.080
Actually, even if he refuses,
I just want to know why!

03:49.560 --> 03:53.740
You're his <i>friend</i>! Could you ask him for me?!

03:58.010 --> 03:59.750
Morning, Iwakura-san.

03:59.750 --> 04:02.060
You're here later than usual today.

04:02.060 --> 04:03.080
Yeah...

04:03.080 --> 04:05.330
My perfect morning...

04:05.750 --> 04:07.470
Morning, Mitsumi-chan.

04:07.800 --> 04:09.990
Good morning, Shima-kun, Mukai-kun.

04:09.990 --> 04:11.450
Just now, I...

04:14.830 --> 04:17.640
I saw Terada-sensei doing
squats in the courtyard!

04:17.640 --> 04:19.260
We should learn from his example!

04:19.260 --> 04:22.190
I'm not sure I want to.

04:23.120 --> 04:24.700
Wait, wait.

04:24.700 --> 04:26.830
He was on TV, right?

04:26.830 --> 04:30.290
If I were him, I would've
bragged about it in my self-intro.

04:31.370 --> 04:33.310
But since he didn't mention it,

04:33.310 --> 04:36.310
maybe he doesn't want anyone to know.

04:36.310 --> 04:37.080
Given that...

04:37.080 --> 04:39.450
I saw your little show.

04:39.450 --> 04:42.460
So, why aren't you joining
the drama club, again?

04:43.410 --> 04:45.840
I can't bring it up!
It'd be tactless as all hell!

04:47.160 --> 04:50.350
Time's up! Pass your papers forward!

04:55.310 --> 04:58.610
I've never seen anyone get
so depressed over a quiz.

04:58.610 --> 04:59.690
Me neither.

05:01.320 --> 05:02.140
Mitsumi?

05:02.140 --> 05:04.320
Our next class is this way.

05:04.320 --> 05:06.110
I don't know the answer.

05:06.110 --> 05:07.320
Mitsumi?

05:08.660 --> 05:09.740
Mitsumi!

05:09.740 --> 05:12.420
It looks like Iwakura-san's
not feeling too well.

05:12.420 --> 05:14.000
You okay?

05:14.000 --> 05:16.250
Take the rest of the class off
and go rest in the infirmary.

05:16.790 --> 05:18.580
Eggscuse me.

05:19.820 --> 05:21.660
The nurse isn't in, huh?

05:24.560 --> 05:26.540
I'm hopeless.

05:26.540 --> 05:29.590
I'm so distracted by this one thing,
I'm messing up everything else.

05:30.630 --> 05:31.260
Boo!

05:31.260 --> 05:31.970
Whoa!

05:33.180 --> 05:35.040
That scared me!

05:35.040 --> 05:36.630
Why are you here?

05:36.630 --> 05:38.370
The boys are playing soccer over there.

05:38.370 --> 05:40.900
I came here to drink some water,
and then I saw you.

05:41.320 --> 05:42.990
So, what happened to you?

05:42.990 --> 05:44.900
I got hit in the face by a volleyball.

05:44.900 --> 05:46.400
What? You okay?

05:46.740 --> 05:47.910
Yeah, the nosebleed stopped immediately.

05:47.910 --> 05:49.800
Oh, is this my chance to ask him?
Yeah, the nosebleed stopped immediately.

05:49.800 --> 05:50.760
Oh, is this my chance to ask him?

05:50.760 --> 05:52.580
Let's try slipping it in casually.

05:53.160 --> 05:55.510
Did you watch that TV show yesterday?

05:55.510 --> 05:58.110
Nope. Was there something good on?

05:58.110 --> 06:00.610
Heh. I didn't watch it either.

06:02.280 --> 06:05.710
You've been acting weird today.
Is something wrong?

06:10.020 --> 06:12.220
Sorry, the thing is...

06:13.160 --> 06:14.970
I see now.

06:14.970 --> 06:17.070
Senpai's up to his tricks, huh?

06:17.070 --> 06:19.980
Oh, but don't be too mad at him.

06:19.980 --> 06:22.710
I did think he was being a little pushy,

06:22.710 --> 06:26.990
but it felt like Kanechika-senpai's just
trying to do whatever he can for his club.

06:28.780 --> 06:31.340
Well, it's not a big deal.

06:31.340 --> 06:33.500
It was gonna get out eventually.

06:33.500 --> 06:37.170
And people who went to my middle school,
like Mukai, already know anyway.

06:37.170 --> 06:38.370
Oh, huh.

06:38.780 --> 06:42.530
With all due respect to Senpai,
I don't wanna act anymore.

06:42.530 --> 06:46.920
I did give it my all back then,
not because I found it fun...

06:48.670 --> 06:51.160
but because it made my mom happy.

06:54.060 --> 06:55.500
How about you?

06:55.500 --> 06:59.170
What made you come to Tokyo
to try to join the government?

06:59.170 --> 07:02.690
That thing you said was a joke, right?
About being born to lead or whatever.

07:03.070 --> 07:05.190
Forget about that already!

07:05.190 --> 07:10.950
Well, my hometown's a great place.
Beautiful landscape and ocean views.

07:11.430 --> 07:13.840
But it's pretty badly underpopulated.

07:14.450 --> 07:17.570
I could have stayed there and helped,

07:17.570 --> 07:21.400
but Japan's full of places like that, right?

07:21.400 --> 07:26.840
If I can, I want to tackle
the problem at its core.

07:26.840 --> 07:30.590
I mean, I'm like my
hometown's biggest prodigy!

07:30.590 --> 07:34.300
You don't need to laugh it off.
I think that's a great goal.

07:37.140 --> 07:39.860
Thanks. I'll do my best.

07:39.860 --> 07:40.730
Great.

07:41.470 --> 07:44.760
You and Kanechika-senpai are amazing.

07:44.760 --> 07:48.270
Nah, I'm really just doing it for myself.

07:48.270 --> 07:54.660
But putting your goal out there means
dealing with hopes and expectations, right?

07:55.810 --> 07:59.560
I couldn't handle it,
pathetic as it may sound.

08:03.700 --> 08:04.420
I...

08:04.420 --> 08:08.410
I nearly let the pressure get to me, too!

08:08.410 --> 08:09.220
Really?

08:09.220 --> 08:10.300
Really!

08:10.300 --> 08:14.930
I was so afraid of failing my entrance
exams, I couldn't even eat for a while!

08:14.930 --> 08:17.630
I would've lost my mind
if it weren't for Fumi!

08:17.630 --> 08:18.470
Fumi?

08:18.470 --> 08:21.680
Oh, she's my best friend.
We grew up together.

08:22.300 --> 08:24.190
Evening!

08:24.190 --> 08:27.750
Let's go grab some gyoza, Mitsumi-chan.

08:27.750 --> 08:28.820
Nope.

08:28.820 --> 08:31.370
What if I forget this vocab while eating?

08:31.370 --> 08:34.710
Yeah, yeah, you'll be fine.

08:34.710 --> 08:36.570
Pops is waiting outside.

08:36.570 --> 08:37.950
Just get in the car.

08:39.080 --> 08:40.160
Here you are.

08:40.160 --> 08:42.680
Wow, there it is!

08:42.680 --> 08:44.560
Lemme divvy up the fried rice.

08:46.760 --> 08:48.850
Once you're done with your exams,

08:49.340 --> 08:53.520
let's come back here for gyoza. Pass or fail.

08:53.520 --> 08:55.540
There's nothing worth celebrating if I fail.

08:55.540 --> 08:58.350
Hah! In society's eyes, maybe.

08:58.670 --> 09:02.730
But having taken up the challenge
will be worth a whole lot to you,

09:02.730 --> 09:05.480
and to me, too, because
I know how hard you're trying.

09:42.340 --> 09:43.430
S'good.

09:43.430 --> 09:44.910
Right?

09:48.540 --> 09:50.860
Even if I'm only doing this for myself,

09:50.860 --> 09:54.400
it made me happy to have a friend
know and watch over me.

09:54.400 --> 09:56.160
Sounds like a good friend.

09:56.160 --> 09:56.910
Yeah!

09:57.750 --> 09:59.110
Lucky you.

09:59.580 --> 10:01.700
We can do the same, then!

10:01.700 --> 10:05.200
If you ever find a goal for yourself,

10:05.200 --> 10:09.210
then, succeed or fail, we'll go anywhere
you want and eat some good food!

10:13.400 --> 10:14.960
That's a promise, okay?

10:17.130 --> 10:18.430
Okay.

10:18.430 --> 10:20.840
He's not going to join. Absolutely not.

10:20.840 --> 10:22.220
Aww!

10:22.220 --> 10:23.460
There you have it.

10:23.460 --> 10:25.980
But why? He told you, right?

10:25.980 --> 10:28.900
Yes, but I can't tell you.
A good friend wouldn't do that.

10:30.670 --> 10:34.020
Let him know he's always welcome
if he ever changes his mind!

10:35.090 --> 10:37.800
Yeah, we're friends...

10:39.890 --> 10:41.530
That's a promise, okay?

10:43.410 --> 10:47.950
So why does my pinky feel all tingly?

10:54.760 --> 10:56.460
Long time no see, everyone.

10:56.460 --> 10:58.040
Morning, Mitsumi.

10:58.040 --> 10:59.170
Been a while, huh?

10:59.170 --> 11:00.260
Good morning.

11:00.260 --> 11:03.100
You look like you made the most
out of the Golden Week holidays.

11:03.100 --> 11:04.430
You can tell?

11:04.430 --> 11:08.210
My aunt showed me all over Tokyo!

11:08.210 --> 11:11.050
Oh, right. You're still new here.

11:11.050 --> 11:13.330
And she helped you pick out
some new clothes, too?

11:13.330 --> 11:14.730
Good for you.

11:14.730 --> 11:16.550
What'd you guys do over the break?

11:16.550 --> 11:19.700
I was too busy studying for midterms,
so I didn't go anywhere.

11:19.700 --> 11:20.610
Same here.

11:20.940 --> 11:21.860
Huh?

11:21.860 --> 11:24.380
You're cramming for exams already?

11:24.380 --> 11:25.830
Nope! Not me!

11:25.830 --> 11:27.580
You and your living-abroad experience.

11:27.580 --> 11:29.430
Must be nice not having to study English.

11:29.430 --> 11:31.830
You're not getting any help from me
if you're gonna be like that.

11:31.830 --> 11:33.640
You've lived abroad, Yuzu-chan?

11:33.640 --> 11:35.200
Whoa, cool!

11:35.200 --> 11:38.710
It was only until third grade.
I still have to grind vocab like you guys.

11:39.050 --> 11:41.540
This school sure has a lot of
students who've lived abroad.

11:41.540 --> 11:42.470
It does?

11:42.470 --> 11:44.850
I hear there are a couple
or so in each class.

11:46.260 --> 11:50.100
I thought I was disciplined.

11:50.570 --> 11:54.110
But I've lost control of myself
ever since getting into high school.

11:54.110 --> 11:56.230
Now I don't know what to do.

11:56.230 --> 11:58.480
She's so damn square.

11:58.480 --> 12:00.870
I think you have the right mindset.

12:00.870 --> 12:02.240
Let's see...

12:02.240 --> 12:04.970
She scored the highest in the entrance
exams without going to cram school,

12:04.970 --> 12:07.140
and she was in the top 20
in the recent tests.

12:07.140 --> 12:09.670
What in the world is she worried about?

12:09.670 --> 12:12.940
That said, it's good that
she's staying on her toes.

12:12.940 --> 12:13.750
Oh.

12:14.140 --> 12:16.630
You've joined the Tsubame Society?

12:16.630 --> 12:17.840
Yes.

12:17.840 --> 12:20.010
Then you know someone who's
the definition of disciplined!

12:20.850 --> 12:22.170
Not happening.

12:22.170 --> 12:24.710
I can't accept these budget cuts.

12:24.710 --> 12:27.020
You know we're taking this seriously!

12:27.020 --> 12:30.150
Many clubs take their activities seriously.

12:30.150 --> 12:33.730
Which is why we took another look at
the budget, taking results into account,

12:33.730 --> 12:37.690
and concluded that the cultural
clubs were underfunded.

12:37.690 --> 12:40.230
Segawa-san, as the soccer
team's future captain,

12:40.230 --> 12:42.370
you should try to spend
your budget more wisely.

12:42.370 --> 12:44.780
We can barely make do
with the <i>current</i> budget!

12:44.780 --> 12:48.360
Also, we're starting to do
better in tournaments!

12:48.360 --> 12:51.640
We found no concrete evidence of that.

12:52.090 --> 12:54.790
As I said, if you write a report
supporting your case, we'll consider it.

12:55.150 --> 12:56.940
Where is it?

12:58.210 --> 12:59.880
You'll pay for this!

13:05.150 --> 13:07.910
We met in the student council
office the other day. Er...

13:07.910 --> 13:12.020
I'm Iwakura—No, please call me
Mitsumi, Takamine-senpai!

13:12.770 --> 13:16.740
I've been trying to get rid
of the slacker within me.

13:17.150 --> 13:18.740
When I went to Hanazono-sensei,

13:18.740 --> 13:23.090
she said nobody in this school
is as disciplined as you!

13:23.090 --> 13:27.910
If you don't mind, would you let me
help with your student council work?!

13:27.910 --> 13:29.030
Sensei said that?

13:31.200 --> 13:32.520
Ahem.

13:32.520 --> 13:35.620
I-If you insist, far be it from me to refuse!

13:35.620 --> 13:37.420
Thank you so much!

13:41.030 --> 13:46.170
Hanazono-sensei's gotta be
the biggest slacker in the faculty here.

13:57.600 --> 14:00.780
I want to take the express that leaves
at six past the hour and transfer to a bus,

14:00.780 --> 14:01.980
which means I should leave now.

14:02.300 --> 14:04.370
Council Member Okada-san's sick today,

14:04.370 --> 14:06.980
so I'll stop by Noyama-san's place instead.

14:06.980 --> 14:11.160
It's just to say hi and drop off this
paperwork, so join me, Mitsumi-san.

14:11.160 --> 14:11.990
Yes, ma'am!

14:11.990 --> 14:15.500
A lecture on urban farming?

14:15.500 --> 14:18.410
I had no idea students did
planning for things like this.

14:18.410 --> 14:20.550
It isn't that surprising.

14:20.550 --> 14:24.200
Some schools even have their students
plan their own school trips.

14:24.200 --> 14:25.300
What?!

14:26.190 --> 14:28.050
When do they study?

14:28.050 --> 14:31.260
The reality is, some people are naturally
gifted, and some just work hard.

14:31.600 --> 14:35.460
Personally, I recognized that
I can't keep up unless I work hard.

14:35.460 --> 14:37.520
That's why I started keeping this schedule.

14:37.520 --> 14:39.270
I-I see.

14:39.270 --> 14:42.490
Objective self-analysis
and tireless hard work.

14:42.490 --> 14:44.190
You're so cool, Senpai!

14:44.190 --> 14:45.780
A-Am I?

14:46.960 --> 14:48.500
I can't tell her that my disposition

14:48.500 --> 14:51.240
leads to weekly nightmares about
missing a bus or train and crying, but...

14:51.240 --> 14:53.440
Don't leave me!
leads to weekly nightmares about
missing a bus or train and crying, but...

14:53.440 --> 14:54.030
Don't leave me!

14:55.130 --> 14:58.870
I'm happy I found someone
who truly understands!

14:59.290 --> 15:00.950
As her senpai, I must put her
on the right path!

15:00.950 --> 15:02.600
Do you want a gummy?
I bought some this morning.
As her senpai, I must put her
on the right path!

15:02.600 --> 15:03.870
Do you want a gummy?
I bought some this morning.

15:03.870 --> 15:05.540
It's times like these, Mitsumi-san!

15:05.540 --> 15:06.460
Huh?

15:06.460 --> 15:11.690
From watching you today, I've noticed
that you have the tendency to space out.

15:11.690 --> 15:12.930
I-I do?!

15:12.930 --> 15:14.850
Do you have any study material on you?

15:14.850 --> 15:15.690
Yes!

15:15.690 --> 15:17.430
Don't waste your travel time.

15:17.820 --> 15:21.020
Make the most of each moment,
so you don't have any regrets!

15:21.020 --> 15:21.940
Yes!

15:21.940 --> 15:24.230
No regrets!

15:26.680 --> 15:28.390
See you again.

15:28.390 --> 15:30.570
Yes. We'll be leaving now.

15:30.570 --> 15:33.270
That took longer than expected.

15:33.270 --> 15:35.200
Oh, no! The bus leaves in two minutes!

15:35.540 --> 15:36.530
Mitsumi-san!

15:36.530 --> 15:39.700
Do you think Noyama-san's farm is that way?

15:41.460 --> 15:43.380
We can find out some other time!

15:43.380 --> 15:45.110
If we run, we might still make the bus!

15:45.110 --> 15:46.290
O-Okay!

15:46.290 --> 15:48.850
I nearly forgot! Discipline!

15:52.790 --> 15:55.100
The next bus isn't for another fifteen minutes.

15:55.100 --> 15:56.880
Ugh, my stomach hurts!

15:56.880 --> 15:59.460
I was supposed to have finished
shopping for study guides in Shibuya—

15:59.460 --> 16:00.350
Senpai.

16:02.950 --> 16:04.890
Wha? Where did you get that?!

16:04.890 --> 16:06.610
He was just over there.

16:07.070 --> 16:09.740
This must be a house cat, right?
He's really friendly.

16:09.740 --> 16:10.090
Where did he come from?

16:10.090 --> 16:11.620
It's like... Mitsumi-san seems diligent,
Where did he come from?

16:11.620 --> 16:13.450
It's like... Mitsumi-san seems diligent,

16:13.450 --> 16:15.110
but deep down, she's...

16:15.110 --> 16:19.370
It's amazing that buses show up
every fifteen minutes here!

16:19.370 --> 16:21.960
That'll go by in a flash
playing with this guy.

16:26.810 --> 16:30.290
Well, it's not like panicking
will make the bus come any faster.

16:30.290 --> 16:32.880
Taro-chan! Where are you?

16:32.880 --> 16:37.550
Thank you! I guess he
just slipped out the door.

16:37.550 --> 16:39.060
Have these, if you'd like.

16:39.060 --> 16:40.510
Thank you.

16:40.510 --> 16:43.560
There's lots of traffic here,
so I'm glad you found him.

16:46.860 --> 16:49.650
I lost 63 minutes!

16:49.650 --> 16:53.910
Can I get back on track by at least
studying geography on this bus?

16:53.910 --> 16:55.910
Rainfall in Southeast Asia,

16:55.910 --> 16:56.650
and then memorize...

16:56.650 --> 16:57.590
Wow! Look, Senpai!
and then memorize...

16:57.590 --> 16:59.580
Wow! Look, Senpai!

16:59.580 --> 17:00.410
What now?!

17:08.520 --> 17:11.800
I didn't know even Tokyo
had this kind of scenery.

17:25.390 --> 17:27.400
Sorry, I did it again!

17:27.400 --> 17:28.890
I'll memorize some vocab.

17:35.150 --> 17:38.090
Oh, well.

17:38.090 --> 17:40.010
Days like this aren't too bad in moderation.

17:43.790 --> 17:46.870
Takamine-senpai is so amazing!

17:46.870 --> 17:49.000
She's like some hotshot CEO!

17:49.410 --> 17:52.420
"Make the most of each moment,
so you don't have any regrets!"

17:52.780 --> 17:55.380
Maybe I should make a schedule, too.

17:55.380 --> 17:58.980
First, I need to take a closer look
at my usual time-wasters.

17:58.980 --> 18:01.480
Decide what food to get at the
convenience store in three minutes.

18:01.480 --> 18:04.420
I'll need that decision-making
ability for government work.

18:04.920 --> 18:08.050
I should use recess to study, too.

18:08.050 --> 18:11.970
Asking friends and teachers for help
will build my communication skills.

18:11.970 --> 18:15.900
Should I turn down one in three
invitations to hang out?

18:15.900 --> 18:18.780
Hmm, I guess it depends on the details.

18:18.780 --> 18:21.570
My calls home run pretty long.

18:21.570 --> 18:25.790
But they worry about me.
I can't call that wasted time.

18:25.790 --> 18:29.430
That time I spent with
Fumi was indispensable, too.

18:29.430 --> 18:32.290
But can I only say that because
it worked out in the end?

18:33.660 --> 18:35.790
What does having no regrets even mean?!

18:42.330 --> 18:43.680
Wait!

18:43.680 --> 18:46.950
Don't leave me!

19:33.470 --> 19:35.730
Oh, good morning, Shima-kun.

19:35.730 --> 19:36.830
Morning.

19:36.830 --> 19:38.790
Whoa, what's with those bags?

19:38.790 --> 19:40.490
Oh, they're that bad, huh?

19:40.840 --> 19:44.100
I was up late coming up with a schedule.

19:44.530 --> 19:45.620
A schedule?

19:46.040 --> 19:50.090
I thought I'd give what I learned
from Takamine-senpai a shot.

19:50.090 --> 19:53.120
Wow. <i>Wow.</i>

19:53.120 --> 19:55.470
Not great if you're losing sleep, though.

19:55.470 --> 19:57.810
I'm just not used to it yet.

19:59.130 --> 20:01.130
Takamine-senpai!

20:01.130 --> 20:03.510
Good morning!

20:05.480 --> 20:06.390
Senpai?

20:06.390 --> 20:07.450
Ahem.

20:07.450 --> 20:09.930
Forgive me. Good morning,
Mitsumi-san, Shima-kun.

20:09.930 --> 20:12.050
Thank you for yesterday.

20:12.050 --> 20:13.870
I learned a lot from you!

20:13.870 --> 20:15.940
Right. About that...

20:16.270 --> 20:18.990
I don't think it's a good idea
to follow my lead.

20:19.820 --> 20:22.340
I was too ashamed to mention it,

20:22.340 --> 20:25.030
but I failed to get into my
preferred middle school.

20:25.570 --> 20:29.280
Sometimes, I do think about the what-ifs,

20:29.280 --> 20:32.410
but I've come to enjoy my high school life.

20:32.890 --> 20:39.300
You never find out where you made the best
use of your time until much later in life.

20:39.300 --> 20:44.220
So ultimately, I think what matters
is to decide how you spend it yourself.

20:45.550 --> 20:47.050
Takamine!

20:47.050 --> 20:49.480
I brought your stupid paperwork!

20:49.480 --> 20:51.950
The soccer team's achievements
over the past few years!

20:51.950 --> 20:54.540
Member count!
All the data you could ever want!

20:54.540 --> 20:55.650
Well? You can't complain now!

20:55.650 --> 20:56.400
I certainly cannot.
Well? You can't complain now!

20:56.400 --> 20:57.090
I certainly cannot.

20:57.090 --> 20:59.420
I'll go through this today
and take it into account.

21:00.200 --> 21:02.690
Is it okay if I get back to you
tomorrow or the day after?

21:03.610 --> 21:04.570
You sure?

21:04.570 --> 21:06.200
Hmm? Of course.

21:06.200 --> 21:09.550
This data is very well organized.

21:09.550 --> 21:11.330
Did you do this yourself, Segawa-san?

21:13.870 --> 21:15.330
Yeah, I did!

21:15.330 --> 21:16.120
Huh?

21:16.120 --> 21:18.920
Don't just start smiling
at me out of nowhere!

21:18.920 --> 21:20.080
Segawa?

21:21.460 --> 21:23.500
Where does he find all that energy?

21:25.010 --> 21:27.560
Anyway, I'll see you in the student
council office sometime.

21:29.600 --> 21:32.470
Takamine-senpai really is wonderful.

21:32.470 --> 21:34.390
Yeah, she's cool.

21:34.390 --> 21:37.320
But, hey, you heard her.

21:37.320 --> 21:40.230
You should do things your own way.

21:40.230 --> 21:45.070
But I want to stick to this
after all the time I spent on it.

21:45.070 --> 21:48.550
Yeah, but sticking to a method that
you know isn't gonna work for you?

21:48.550 --> 21:50.580
That's the definition of a waste of time.

21:52.390 --> 21:53.810
So cold!

21:53.810 --> 21:56.060
Your logic is so cold, Shima-kun!

21:56.060 --> 21:57.510
Huh? Yikes, sorry!

21:57.510 --> 21:59.210
I wasn't trying to be a jerk!

21:59.800 --> 22:00.990
C-Cold, but true...

22:00.990 --> 22:02.150
Listen, you've got things going for you!
C-Cold, but true...

22:02.150 --> 22:03.280
Listen, you've got things going for you!

22:03.280 --> 22:08.060
You've got your own pace,
your own style of doing things.
